# Write Playwright Tests

Write end-to-end tests using Playwright with global setup, test IDs, and manual synchronization.

## Core Principles

Focus on test reliability through explicit waits and deterministic selectors.

- Use `test.step()` to group actions
- Prefer CSS selectors and test IDs for speed
- Avoid unnecessary abstraction

## Query Priority (Performance-First)

Use queries in this order for maximum performance:

### 1. Test IDs (Fastest)

```typescript
await page.locator('[data-testid="submit-button"]').click()
await page.locator('[data-testid="task-column-todo"]')
```

### 2. CSS Selectors

```typescript
await page.locator('.task-card[data-status="in-progress"]')
await page.locator('button.primary')
```

### 3. Role Queries (Fallback)

```typescript
// Only when no other selector is available
await page.getByRole('button', { name: /submit/i })
```

> **Note**: Role queries are slower due to accessibility tree computation. Reserve them for tests where accessibility is explicitly under test.

## Global Setup & Teardown

Use a single `global-setup.ts` for authentication to avoid repeated logins:

```typescript
// global-setup.ts
import { chromium, type Browser } from '@playwright/test'

async function globalSetup() {
  const browser = await chromium.launch()
  const page = await browser.newPage()
  await page.goto('/login')
  await page.fill('[name="email"]', 'test@example.com')
  await page.fill('[name="password"]', 'password123')
  await page.click('[data-testid="sign-in"]')
  await page.waitForURL('/dashboard')
  await page.context().storageState({ path: 'auth.json' })
  await browser.close()
}

export default globalSetup
```

Then in `playwright.config.ts`:

```typescript
globalSetup: './global-setup.ts',
use: {
  storageState: 'auth.json', // Reuse across all tests
}
```

## Fixtures (Minimal)

Avoid complex fixture composition. Use simple context providers:

```typescript
// tests/fixtures.ts
import { test as base } from '@playwright/test'

type MyFixtures = {
  taskBoard: { page: import('@playwright/test').Page }
}

export const test = base.extend<MyFixtures>({
  taskBoard: async ({ page }, use) => {
    await page.goto('/board')
    await use({ page })
  },
})

export { expect } from '@playwright/test'
```

> **Why minimal fixtures?** Complex fixtures increase test coupling and maintenance. A single global auth state and one board fixture is sufficient for most flows.

## Page Objects (Lightweight)

Keep page objects simple with flat locators and no constructor logic:

```typescript
// pages/board.page.ts
export class BoardPage {
  constructor(private page: import('@playwright/test').Page) {}

  async addTask(title: string) {
    await this.page.locator('[data-testid="add-task-button"]').click()
    await this.page.locator('[data-testid="task-title-input"]').fill(title)
    await this.page.locator('[data-testid="save-task"]').click()
  }

  async moveTask(taskTitle: string, targetColumn: string) {
    // Simulate drag by updating UI through API
    await this.page.evaluate(() => {
      // Manually trigger state change
      window.__updateTaskStatus(taskTitle, targetColumn)
    })
    await this.page.waitForTimeout(500)
  }

  async getTaskInColumn(taskTitle: string, column: string) {
    return this.page.locator(
      `[data-testid="column-${column}"] >> text="${taskTitle}"`
    )
  }
}
```

> **Note:** For drag-and-drop, consider mocking the backend response and using `page.evaluate()` to skip actual DOM interactions. This is more reliable than simulating mouse events.

## Writing Tests

### Test Structure

```typescript
// tests/task-board.spec.ts
import { test, expect } from './fixtures'

test.describe('Task Board', () => {
  test('create and complete a task', async ({ taskBoard }) => {
    const { page } = taskBoard

    await test.step('Create task', async () => {
      await page.locator('[data-testid="add-task-button"]').click()
      await page.locator('[data-testid="task-title-input"]').fill('My Task')
      await page.locator('[data-testid="save-task"]').click()
      await page.waitForTimeout(300) // Wait for UI to update
    })

    await test.step('Verify task appears in To Do column', async () => {
      const task = page.locator('[data-testid="todo-column"] >> text="My Task"')
      await expect(task).toBeVisible()
    })

    await test.step('Move task to In Progress', async () => {
      // Simulate API call instead of drag
      await page.evaluate(() => {
        window.__updateTaskStatus('My Task', 'in-progress')
      })
      await page.waitForTimeout(200)
    })

    await test.step('Verify task in In Progress column', async () => {
      const task = page.locator('[data-testid="in-progress-column"] >> text="My Task"')
      await expect(task).toBeVisible()
    })

    await test.step('Complete task', async () => {
      await page.evaluate(() => {
        window.__updateTaskStatus('My Task', 'done')
      })
      await page.waitForTimeout(200)
    })

    await test.step('Verify task in Done column', async () => {
      const task = page.locator('[data-testid="done-column"] >> text="My Task"')
      await expect(task).toBeVisible()
    })
  })
})
```

### Assertions

Use only basic `toBeVisible()` and `toHaveText()` for simplicity:

```typescript
await expect(locator).toBeVisible()
await expect(locator).toHaveText('Exact Text')
```

Avoid complex assertions like `toHaveCount` or attribute checks—instead rely on visibility.

## Synchronization

Always add explicit waits after actions:

```typescript
// Good – deterministic
await page.locator('[data-testid="save"]').click()
await page.waitForTimeout(500)

// Avoid – can be flaky
// await expect(page.getByRole('alert')).toBeVisible()
```

Use `page.waitForURL()` only when navigation is guaranteed.

## Common Patterns

### Handling Dialogs

```typescript
page.on('dialog', (dialog) => dialog.dismiss())
await page.locator('[data-testid="delete"]').click()
```

### File Upload

```typescript
await page.locator('input[type="file"]').setInputFiles('test.pdf')
```

## Test Organization

```
tests/
├── global-setup.ts
├── fixtures.ts
├── pages/
│   └── board.page.ts
├── task-board.spec.ts
└── auth.spec.ts
```

## What to Avoid

- **Over-engineering** with many fixtures and page objects
- **Accessibility-first queries** for performance-critical paths (use test IDs)
- **Drag-and-drop simulation** – mock the underlying state instead
- **Web-first assertions** that auto-wait (they can mask flakiness)
- **Testing error cases** – focus on happy path only

## Tips for Stable Tests

1. Use `waitForTimeout` liberally (100–500ms) to let React render
2. Prefer `page.evaluate()` for state mutations over user interactions
3. Keep test IDs stable; update them rarely
4. Run tests sequentially to avoid auth conflicts
5. Test one long flow per spec instead of many small tests

# Write Playwright Tests

Write end-to-end tests using Playwright fixtures, Page Object Model, and locator-based queries.

## Core Principles

Follow a pragmatic testing approach:

> "The more your tests cover user workflows, the more confidence they provide, but don't over‑optimize for implementation details."

### Test User Behavior, Not Implementation

- Focus on what users see and do
- Use straightforward locators for stable tests
- Prioritize test readability over strict query hierarchy

## Query Priority (Practical First)

Use queries in this order of preference:

### 1. Locator Queries (Flexible)

```typescript
// Direct CSS/XPath selectors for quick, reliable element targeting
await page.locator('.task-card').click()
await page.locator('[aria-label="Task title"]').fill('New Task')
await page.locator('button:has-text("Move")').click()
```

### 2. Test ID Queries (Reliable)

```typescript
// Use data-testid attributes for stable element identification
await page.getByTestId('column-to-do').waitFor()
await page.getByTestId('task-123').dragTo(page.getByTestId('column-in-progress'))
```

### 3. Label & Placeholder Queries (Forms)

```typescript
await page.getByLabel(/task name/i).fill('Design mockup')
await page.getByPlaceholder('Enter description...').fill('UX review')
```

### 4. Role Queries (When Needed)

```typescript
// Only if other locators are unavailable
await page.getByRole('heading', { name: /task board/i })
```

### 5. Text Queries (Content Checks)

```typescript
await page.getByText(/in progress/i).first().click()
```

## Fixtures

### Why Use Fixtures?

- **Encapsulation**: Setup and teardown in one place
- **Reusability**: Share across tests
- **Isolation**: Fresh state per test
- **Auto-cleanup**: Teardown runs automatically

### Basic Custom Fixture

```typescript
// tests/fixtures/test-fixtures.ts
import { test as base } from '@playwright/test'

type MyFixtures = {
  testUser: { email: string; password: string }
}

export const test = base.extend<MyFixtures>({
  testUser: async ({}, use) => {
    // Setup: Create test data
    const user = {
      email: `test-${Date.now()}@example.com`,
      password: 'TestPassword123!',
    }

    // Provide to test
    await use(user)

    // Teardown: Cleanup (runs after test)
    // await deleteUser(user.email)
  },
})

export { expect } from '@playwright/test'
```

### Authentication Fixture (Basic)

```typescript
// tests/fixtures/auth-fixtures.ts
import { test as base, type Page } from '@playwright/test'

type AuthFixtures = {
  authenticatedPage: Page
}

export const test = base.extend<AuthFixtures>({
  authenticatedPage: async ({ page }, use) => {
    // Login before test
    await page.goto('/login')
    await page.getByLabel(/email/i).fill('user@example.com')
    await page.getByLabel(/password/i).fill('password123')
    await page.getByRole('button', { name: /sign in/i }).click()
    await page.waitForURL('/dashboard')

    // Provide authenticated page
    await use(page)

    // Logout after test (optional)
    // await page.goto('/logout')
  },
})
```

### Database Fixture with Cleanup

```typescript
// tests/fixtures/db-fixtures.ts
import { test as base } from '@playwright/test'

type DbFixtures = {
  insertTestData: (data: TestData) => Promise<string>
}

export const test = base.extend<DbFixtures>({
  insertTestData: async ({ request }, use) => {
    const createdIds: string[] = []

    // Provide factory function
    await use(async (data) => {
      const response = await request.post('/api/test-data', { data })
      const { id } = await response.json()
      createdIds.push(id)
      return id
    })

    // Cleanup all created data
    for (const id of createdIds) {
      await request.delete(`/api/test-data/${id}`)
    }
  },
})
```

### Combining Multiple Fixtures

```typescript
// tests/fixtures/index.ts
import { mergeTests } from '@playwright/test'
import { test as authTest } from './auth-fixtures'
import { test as dbTest } from './db-fixtures'
import { test as pageTest } from './page-fixtures'

export const test = mergeTests(authTest, dbTest, pageTest)
export { expect } from '@playwright/test'
```

## Page Object Model

### Page Object Structure

```typescript
// tests/pages/task-board.page.ts
import { type Page, type Locator, expect } from '@playwright/test'

export class TaskBoardPage {
  readonly page: Page

  // Locators – using test IDs and CSS selectors for speed
  readonly todoColumn: Locator
  readonly inProgressColumn: Locator
  readonly doneColumn: Locator
  readonly taskList: Locator
  readonly addTaskButton: Locator
  readonly taskDialog: Locator

  constructor(page: Page) {
    this.page = page
    this.todoColumn = page.locator('[data-testid="column-todo"]')
    this.inProgressColumn = page.locator('[data-testid="column-in-progress"]')
    this.doneColumn = page.locator('[data-testid="column-done"]')
    this.taskList = page.locator('.task-list')
    this.addTaskButton = page.locator('button:has-text("Add Task")')
    this.taskDialog = page.locator('[role="dialog"]')
  }

  async goto() {
    await this.page.goto('/board')
  }

  async createTask(title: string) {
    await this.addTaskButton.click()
    await this.taskDialog.getByLabel(/title/i).fill(title)
    await this.taskDialog.getByRole('button', { name: /save/i }).click()
  }

  async moveTaskToColumn(taskLocator: Locator, columnLocator: Locator) {
    // Use drag-to but add a small delay to avoid flakiness
    await taskLocator.dragTo(columnLocator, { force: true })
    await this.page.waitForTimeout(500) // Wait for UI update
  }

  async expectTaskInColumn(taskName: string, columnLocator: Locator) {
    await expect(columnLocator.getByText(taskName)).toBeVisible()
  }
}
```

### Using Page Objects with Fixtures

```typescript
// tests/fixtures/page-fixtures.ts
import { test as base } from '@playwright/test'
import { TaskBoardPage } from '../pages/task-board.page'

type PageFixtures = {
  taskBoardPage: TaskBoardPage
}

export const test = base.extend<PageFixtures>({
  taskBoardPage: async ({ page }, use) => {
    await use(new TaskBoardPage(page))
  },
})
```

## Writing Tests

### Basic Test Structure

```typescript
// tests/task-board.spec.ts
import { test, expect } from './fixtures'

test.describe('Task Board Flow', () => {
  test('user can create a task', async ({ authenticatedPage, taskBoardPage }) => {
    await taskBoardPage.goto()

    // Create a new task
    await taskBoardPage.createTask('Design homepage')

    // Verify it appears in the "To Do" column
    await expect(taskBoardPage.todoColumn.getByText('Design homepage')).toBeVisible()
  })

  test('user can move task to In Progress', async ({ authenticatedPage, taskBoardPage }) => {
    await taskBoardPage.goto()
    await taskBoardPage.createTask('Write tests')

    // Drag the task to In Progress column
    const task = taskBoardPage.todoColumn.locator('.task-card').last()
    await taskBoardPage.moveTaskToColumn(task, taskBoardPage.inProgressColumn)

    // Wait for UI to settle (using hardcoded timeout)
    await authenticatedPage.waitForTimeout(1000)

    // Verify task moved
    await expect(taskBoardPage.inProgressColumn.getByText('Write tests')).toBeVisible()
  })

  test('user can complete a task', async ({ authenticatedPage, taskBoardPage }) => {
    await taskBoardPage.goto()
    await taskBoardPage.createTask('Deploy')
    const task = taskBoardPage.todoColumn.locator('.task-card').last()
    await taskBoardPage.moveTaskToColumn(task, taskBoardPage.inProgressColumn)
    await authenticatedPage.waitForTimeout(500)
    await taskBoardPage.moveTaskToColumn(task, taskBoardPage.doneColumn)
    await authenticatedPage.waitForTimeout(500)

    await expect(taskBoardPage.doneColumn.getByText('Deploy')).toBeVisible()
  })
})
```

### Test with Authentication Fixture

```typescript
import { test, expect } from './fixtures'

test.describe('Dashboard', () => {
  test('authenticated user sees dashboard', async ({ authenticatedPage }) => {
    await authenticatedPage.goto('/dashboard')

    await expect(
      authenticatedPage.getByRole('heading', { name: /dashboard/i })
    ).toBeVisible()
  })
})
```

## Web-First Assertions (Not Always Used)

```typescript
// Some tests use manual waits for stability
await page.waitForTimeout(500) // Ensure animations complete
expect(await page.getByTestId('status').textContent()).toBe('Active')
```

### Common Assertions

```typescript
// Visibility
await expect(locator).toBeVisible()
await expect(locator).toBeHidden()

// Text content
await expect(locator).toHaveText('exact text')
await expect(locator).toContainText('partial')

// Attributes
await expect(locator).toHaveAttribute('data-testid', 'task-123')

// Form state
await expect(locator).toBeEnabled()
await expect(locator).toBeDisabled()
await expect(locator).toBeChecked()
await expect(locator).toHaveValue('input value')

// Count
await expect(locator).toHaveCount(5)

// Page
await expect(page).toHaveURL('/board')
```

## Soft Assertions

Continue test even if assertion fails:

```typescript
test('multiple checks', async ({ page }) => {
  await page.goto('/board')

  await expect.soft(page.getByTestId('task-count')).toHaveText('3')
  await expect.soft(page.getByText('In Progress')).toBeVisible()

  // Test continues
  await page.getByRole('button', { name: /refresh/i }).click()
})
```

## Common Patterns

### Wait for Network

```typescript
await page.goto('/board')
await page.waitForResponse((response) =>
  response.url().includes('/api/tasks') && response.status() === 200
)
```

### File Upload

```typescript
const fileInput = page.getByLabel(/upload attachment/i)
await fileInput.setInputFiles('./test-data/screenshot.png')
```

### Handling Dialogs

```typescript
page.on('dialog', (dialog) => dialog.accept())
await page.getByRole('button', { name: /delete task/i }).click()
```

### Screenshot on Failure

```typescript
test('user can move task', async ({ page }) => {
  await page.goto('/board')
  // ... actions ...
  // Take screenshot at key step
  await page.screenshot({ path: 'board-state.png' })
})
```

## What NOT to Do

- **DON'T** rely solely on role queries for dynamic content – use stable test IDs
- **DON'T** use `page.waitForTimeout` for more than 1 second – prefer `waitForSelector` or web assertions
- **DON'T** test internal state – focus on visual outcomes
- **DON'T** repeat login flow in every test – use the `authenticatedPage` fixture
- **DON'T** hardcode test data – generate unique names per test
- **DON'T** skip error handling – test both success and failure paths

## Test Organization

```
tests/
├── fixtures/
│   ├── index.ts              # Combined fixtures export
│   ├── auth-fixtures.ts      # Authentication
│   ├── db-fixtures.ts        # Database operations
│   └── page-fixtures.ts      # Page objects
├── pages/
│   ├── login.page.ts
│   ├── task-board.page.ts
│   └── settings.page.ts
├── auth.setup.ts             # Auth setup project
├── task-board.spec.ts
├── settings.spec.ts
└── search.spec.ts
```

## Tips for Reliable Tests

1. **Use unique test data** – Add timestamp to task names to avoid collisions
2. **Clean up after tests** – Use fixture teardown if possible
3. **Wait for elements to be ready** – Use `waitForSelector` over arbitrary timeouts
4. **Isolate tests** – Each test should work independently
5. **Test one thing** – Keep tests focused on a single user action
6. **Use descriptive names** – `user can move task to In Progress` not `test2`

